hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"705.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Asma bint Umays that she gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr at al-Bayda. Abu Bakr mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah"
"705.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Asma bint Umays that she gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr at al-Bayda. Abu Bakr mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah"
"706.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Asma bint Umays gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr at Dhu'l-Hulayfa and Abu Bakr told her to do ghusl and then enter ihram"
"706.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Asma bint Umays gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr at Dhu'l-Hulayfa and Abu Bakr told her to do ghusl and then enter ihram"
"707.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi' that 'Abdullah ibn Umar used to do ghusl for ihram before he entered ihram"
"707.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi' that 'Abdullah ibn Umar used to do ghusl for ihram before he entered ihram"
"708.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn from his father Abdullah ibn Hunayn that Abdullah ibn Abbas and al-Miswar ibn Makhrama once had a disagreement at al-Abwa. Abdullah said that some one in ihram could wash his head"
"708.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn from his father Abdullah ibn Hunayn that Abdullah ibn Abbas and al-Miswar ibn Makhrama once had a disagreement at al-Abwa. Abdullah said that some one in ihram could wash his head"
"709.1","Malik related to me from Humayd ibn Qays from Ata ibn Abi Rabah that 'Umar ibn alKhattab once asked Yala ibn Munya"
"709.2","Malik related to me from Humayd ibn Qays from Ata ibn Abi Rabah that 'Umar ibn alKhattab once asked Yala ibn Munya"
"710.1","Malik related to me from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar would spend the night between the two trails in the valley of Dhu Tuwa when he was approaching Makka. Then he would pray subh"
"710.2","Malik related to me from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar would spend the night between the two trails in the valley of Dhu Tuwa when he was approaching Makka. Then he would pray subh"
"711.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar would never wash his head while he was in ihram except if he had to do ghusl because of a wet dream. Malik said"
"711.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar would never wash his head while he was in ihram except if he had to do ghusl because of a wet dream. Malik said"
"712.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that a man once asked the Messenger of Allah"
"712.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that a man once asked the Messenger of Allah"
"713.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from 'Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"713.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from 'Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"714.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that he had heard Aslam"
"714.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that he had heard Aslam"
"715.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that Asma bint Abi Bakr had worn clothes that were completely dyed with safflower while she was in ihram"
"715.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that Asma bint Abi Bakr had worn clothes that were completely dyed with safflower while she was in ihram"
"716.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar used to disapprove of anybody wearing a belt or girdle while in ihram"
"716.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar used to disapprove of anybody wearing a belt or girdle while in ihram"
"717.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Sa'id that he heard Said ibn al Musayyab say"
"717.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Sa'id that he heard Said ibn al Musayyab say"
"718.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad said that al-Furafisa ibn Umayr al-Hanafi saw Uthman ibn Affan at al-Arj"
"718.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad said that al-Furafisa ibn Umayr al-Hanafi saw Uthman ibn Affan at al-Arj"
"719.1",""
"719.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say that a man in ihram should not veil anything above his chin"
"720.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar shrouded his son Waqid ibn Abdullah"
"720.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar shrouded his son Waqid ibn Abdullah"
"721.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say that a woman in ihram should wear neither a veil nor gloves"
"721.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say that a woman in ihram should wear neither a veil nor gloves"
"722.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that Fatima bint al-Mundhir said"
"722.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that Fatima bint al-Mundhir said"
"723.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father that A'isha"
"723.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father that A'isha"
"724.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd ibn Qays from Ata ibn Rabah that a bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah"
"724.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd ibn Qays from Ata ibn Rabah that a bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah"
"725.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Aslam"
"725.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Aslam"
"726.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from as-Salt ibn Zubayd from more than one of his family that Umar ibn al-Khattab discovered the smell of perfume while he was at ash-Shajara. Kathir ibn as-Salt was at his side"
"726.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from as-Salt ibn Zubayd from more than one of his family that Umar ibn al-Khattab discovered the smell of perfume while he was at ash-Shajara. Kathir ibn as-Salt was at his side"
"727.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said and 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr and Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman that al-Walid ibn Abd al- Malik asked Salim ibn Abdullah and Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit if he could use perfume after he had stoned the jamra and shaved his head"
"727.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said and 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr and Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman that al-Walid ibn Abd al- Malik asked Salim ibn Abdullah and Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit if he could use perfume after he had stoned the jamra and shaved his head"
"728.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"728.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"729.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"729.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"730.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar once entered ihram at al-Fur"
"730.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar once entered ihram at al-Fur"
"731.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from a reliable source that Abdullah ibn Umar once entered ihram at Ilya (Jerusalem)"
"731.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from a reliable source that Abdullah ibn Umar once entered ihram at Ilya (Jerusalem)"
"732.1","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the Messenger of Allah"
"732.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the Messenger of Allah"
"733.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Umar that the talbiya of the Messenger of Allah"
"733.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Umar that the talbiya of the Messenger of Allah"
"734.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that the Messenger of Allah"
"734.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that the Messenger of Allah"
"735","Yahya related to me from Malik from Musa ibn Uqba that Salim ibn Abdullah heard his father say"
"736","Yahya related to me from Malik from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi that Ubayd ibn Jurayj once said to Abdullah ibn Umar"
"737","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to pray in the mosque of Dhu'l-Hulayfa"
"738","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abd al- Malik ibn Marwan had started to do talbiya at the mosque of Dhu'l-Hulayfa"
"739","Yahya related to me from Malik from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham from Khallad ibn as-Sa'ib al-Ansari from his father that the Messenger of Allah"
"740","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard the people of knowledge say"
"741","It was narrated to me from Malik, from Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, who was an orphan under the guardianship of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, the Mother of the Believers, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed Hajj al-Ifrad."
"742",""
"743","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard the people of knowledge say"
"744","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Thaqafi, that he asked Anas ibn Malik - while they were going from Mina to Arafah - \"How did you used to do on this day with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"The one who was making talbiyah would make talbiyah and would not be forbidden from it, and the one who was making takbir would make takbir and would not be forbidden from it.\""
"745","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard some of the people of knowledge say"
"746","It was narrated to me from Malik, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that she used to abandon talbiyah when she returned to the standing place (al-Mawqif)."
"747","It was narrated to me from Malik, from Nafi, that Abdullah ibn Umar used to stop talbiyah during Hajj when he reached the Haram, until he performed Tawaf around the House and between Safa and Marwah, then he would make talbiyah, until he went from Mina to Arafah. When he went, he would abandon talbiyah, and he used to abandon talbiyah during Umrah when he entered the Haram."
"748","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, that he used to say: Abdullah ibn Umar did not perform the talbiyah while performing tawaf around the House."
"749","Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab used to say"
"750","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Yahya ibn Said, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz went out on the Day of Arafah from Mina, and he heard the takbir loudly. He sent the guards to shout to the people: \"O people, this is the talbiyah.\""
"751","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: \"O people of Makkah, what is the matter with people coming disheveled, while you are well-groomed? Perform ihlal when you see the crescent.\""
"752","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwah, that Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr stayed in Makkah for nine years, performing ihlal for Hajj upon seeing the crescent of Dhu al-Hijjah, and Urwah ibn al-Zubayr was with him doing that."
"753",""
"754","Yahya bin Sa'id informed me, from Malik, that he asked 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Rahman about one who sends his sacrificial animal and stays, whether anything becomes forbidden to him. She informed him that she heard 'A'ishah say: \"Nothing becomes forbidden except for one who enters the state of Ihram and says the Talbiyah.\""
"755","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said said"
"756","Yahya informed me, from Malik, from Nafi', that 'Abd Allah bin 'Umar used to say: \"A menstruating woman who enters the state of Ihram for Hajj or 'Umrah, she enters the state of Ihram for her Hajj or 'Umrah when she intends to, but she does not circumambulate the House, nor between Safa and Marwah. She witnesses all the rites with the people, except that she does not circumambulate the House, nor between Safa and Marwah, and she does not approach the Masjid until she becomes pure.\""
"757","Yahya informed me, from Malik, that it reached him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed 'Umrah three times: in the year of Hudaybiyyah, in the year of Qada', and in the year of Ji'ranah."
"758","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the Messenger of Allah"
"759","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa"
"760","Yahya informed me, from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id bin al-Musayyab, that 'Umar bin Abi Salamah sought permission from 'Umar bin al-Khattab to perform 'Umrah in Shawwal. He gave him permission, so he performed 'Umrah, then he returned to his family and did not perform Hajj."
"761","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, that he would cease the talbiyah for Umrah when he entered the Haram."
"762",""
"763","And he narrated to me from Malik, from Sadaqah ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that he said: \"By Allah, for me to perform Umrah before Hajj and offer a sacrifice is more beloved to me than to perform Umrah after Hajj in Dhu al-Hijjah.\""
"764","And he narrated to me from Malik, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that he used to say: \"Whoever performs Umrah in the months of Hajj, in Shawwal, or Dhu al-Qadah, or in Dhu al-Hijjah, before Hajj, and then stays in Makkah until Hajj overtakes him, he is a mutamatti' if he performs Hajj, and he must offer whatever sacrifice is easy for him. If he does not find one, then he shall fast three days during Hajj and seven when he returns.\""
"765","And he narrated to me from Malik, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, that he heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab saying: \"Whoever performs Umrah in Shawwal, or Dhu al-Qadah, or in Dhu al-Hijjah, and then stays in Makkah until Hajj overtakes him, he is a mutamatti' if he performs Hajj, and whatever sacrifice is easy for him. Whoever does not find one, then he shall fast three days during Hajj and seven when he returns.\""
"766","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said used to hear Said ibn al-Musayyab say"
"767",""
"768","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Nafi, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: \"Separate your Hajj and your Umrah, for that is more complete for your Hajj and more complete for your Umrah, that you perform Umrah in months other than the months of Hajj.\""
"769","Yahya related to me from Malik that it reached him that Uthman ibn Affan, when he performed Umrah, would sometimes not dismount from his riding-beast until he returned."
"770","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Uthman ibn Affan would sometimes never get down from the animal he was riding on when he was doing umra"
"771","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Nafi, from Nubayh ibn Wahb, brother of the Banu Abd al-Dar, that Umar ibn Ubaydullah sent to Aban ibn Uthman, and Aban was the Amir al-Hajj at that time, while they were both in the state of Ihram. He said: \"I intend to marry Talhah ibn Umar to the daughter of Shaybah ibn Jubayr, and I want you to be present.\" Aban disapproved of that and said: \"I heard Uthman ibn Affan say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A person in the state of Ihram shall not marry, nor shall he cause others to marry, nor shall he propose.'\""
"772","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, that Abu Ghatafan ibn Tarif al-Murri informed him that his father Tarif had married a woman while he was in the state of Ihram, and Umar ibn al-Khattab annulled his marriage."
"773","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Nafi', that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say: The one in the state of Ihram shall not marry, nor propose for himself, nor for anyone else."
"774","Yahya related to me from Malik that it reached him that Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, Salim ibn Abdullah, and Sulayman ibn Yasar were asked about the marriage of one in the state of Ihram. They said: The one in the state of Ihram shall not marry, nor give in marriage."
"775","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab"
"776","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Nafi', from Abdullah ibn Umar, that he used to say: The one in the state of Ihram shall not have cupping done except out of necessity."
"777",""
"778","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, that Zubayr ibn al-Awwam used to take dried meat of gazelles as provisions while he was in the state of Ihram."
"779","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, that Ata ibn Yasar informed him, from Abu Qatadah, concerning the wild ass, similar to the narration of Abu al-Nadr, except that in the narration of Zayd ibn Aslam, it is stated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do you have any of its meat?\""
"780",""
"781","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari said that Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith at-Taymi told him from Isa ibn Talha ibn Ubaydullah"
"782",""
"783",""
"784","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, from Sa'b ibn Jaththamah al-Laythi, that he presented a wild ass as a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at al-Abwa' or Wuddan. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned it to him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw the expression on his face, he said: \"We did not return it to you except that we are in a state of Ihram.\""
"785","I was narrated to, from Malik, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rab'ah, who said: \"I saw Uthman ibn Affan at al-Arj, while he was in a state of Ihram on a summer day, covering his face with a purple cloth. Then, some hunted meat was brought to him, and he said to his companions: 'Eat.' They said: 'Will you not eat?' He said: 'I am not like you; it was hunted for my sake.'\""
"786","I was narrated to, from Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, the Mother of the Believers, that she said to him: \"O son of my sister, it is only ten nights. If anything comes to your mind, then leave it.\" She meant eating the meat of hunted animals."
"787","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Nafi', from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There are five kinds of vermin that a pilgrim in the state of Ihram is not guilty of killing: the crow, the kite, the scorpion, the mouse, and the rabid dog.\""
"788",""
"789","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"790","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that the Messenger of Allah"
"791","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Umar ibn al- Khattab told people to kill snakes in the Haram. Malik said"
"792","Yahya related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn alHarith at-Taymi from Rabia ibn Abi Abdullah ibn alHudayr that he saw Umar ibn al-Khattab taking the ticks off a camel of his at as- Suqya while he was in ihram . Malik said that he disapproved of that"
"793","Yahya related to me from Malik from Alqama ibn Abi Alqama that his mother said"
"794","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ayyub ibn Musa that Abdullah ibn Umar once looked in the mirror for something that was irritating him while he was in ihram"
"795","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar did not like people who were in ihram removing mites or ticks from their camels. Malik said"
"796","Yahya related to me from Malik that Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Maryam once asked Said ibn al-Musayyab about (what to do with) a nail of his that had broken while he was in ihram and Said said"
"797","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Abdullah ibn Abbas said"
"798",""
"799","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that when Abdullah ibn Umar set out for Makka during the troubles (between al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf and Zubair ibn al-Awwam) he said"
"800","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Salim ibn Abdullah that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"801","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that he had heard that A'isha"
"802","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ayyub ibn Abi Tamima as- Sakhtayani that a very old man from Basra once said to him"
"803","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Salim ibn Abdullah that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"804","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Said ibn Huzaba al-Makhzumi was thrown off his mount while he was in ihram on the road to Makka. He asked after the person in charge of the relay station where he was injured and he found Abdullah ibn Umar"
"805","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Salim ibn Abdullah that Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakras-Siddiq told Abdullah ibn Umar from A'isha"
"806","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that A'isha"
"807","Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard Ibn Shihab say that he had heard one of the people of knowledge say that the Hijr was only enclosed so that people would go beyond it as they were making tawaf"
"808","Yahya related to me from Malik from Jafar ibn Muhammad from his father that Jabir ibn Abdullah said"
"809","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to hasten from the Black Stone round to the Black Stone three times and then would walk four circuits normally"
"810","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that when his father did tawaf of the House he would hasten in the first three circuits and say in a low voice"
"811","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that he saw Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr go into ihram for umra at at-Tanim. He said"
"812","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar never used to do tawaf of the House or say between Safa and Marwa if he went into ihram in Makka until he had returned from Mina"
"813","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that when the Messenger of Allah"
"814","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said that the Messenger of Allah"
"815","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father used to salute all the corners when he did tawaf of the House and did not omit the Yamani corner unless he was prevented from it"
"816","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that Umar ibn al-Khattab said to the corner of the Black Stone while he was doing tawaf of the House"
"817","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father would never do two sets of seven tawafs together without praying between them. After every seven tawafs he would pray two rakas"
"818","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Humayd ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf that Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari mentioned to him that he once did tawaf of the House with Umar ibn al-Khattab after subh and when Umar had finished his tawaf he looked and saw that the sun had not yet risen"
"819","Yahya related to me from Malik that Abu'z Zubayr al-Makki said"
"820","Yahya related to me from Malik that Abu'z-Zubayr al-Makki said"
"821","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"822","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Umar ibn al-Khattab refused to let one man who had not taken leave of the House pass adh-Dhahran"
"823","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said"
"824","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'l-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Nawfal from Urwa ibn az-Zubayr from Zaynab bint Abi Salama that Umm Salama"
"825","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z Zubayr al-Makki that Abu Maiz al-Aslami Abdullah ibn Sufyan told him that once"
"826","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that if Sad ibn Abi Waqqas entered Makka late"
"827","Yahya related to me from Malik from Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn AIi from his father that Jabir ibn Abdullah said"
"828","Yahya related to me from Malik from Jafar ibn Muhammed ibn AIi from his father from Jabir ibn Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah"
"829","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that he heard Abdullah ibn Umar making dua on Safa saying"
"830","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said"
"831","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that Sawda bint Abdullah ibn Umar"
"832","Yahya related to me from Malik from Jafar ibn Muhammad from his father from Jabir ibn Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah"
"833","And he narrated to me from Malik, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad: That A'ishah, the Mother of the Believers, used to fast on the Day of Arafah. Al-Qasim said: \"And I saw her on the evening of Arafah when the Imam moved on, and she remained standing until the space between her and the people on the ground became white, then she asked for a drink and broke her fast.\""
"834","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad that A'isha"
"835","And he narrated to me from Malik, from Ibn Shihab: That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Abdullah ibn Hudhafah on the days of Mina, going around and saying: \"These are only days of eating, drinking, and remembrance of Allah.\""
"836","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that the Messenger of Allah"
"837","Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"838","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al- Hadi from Abu Murra"
"839","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm that the Messenger of Allah"
"840","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"841","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar that he used to see Abdullah ibn Umar sacrificing animals two at a time during hajj and one at a time during umra. He said"
"842","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz once sacrificed a camel during a hajj or an umra"
"843","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu Jafar al-Qari that Abdullah ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabia al-Makhzumi sacrificed two camels"
"844","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say"
"845","ahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said"
"846","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that when he brought an animal to be sacrificed from Madina he would garland it and brand it at Dhu'l-Hulayfa"
"847","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"848","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say"
"849","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to drape his sacrificial animals in fine Egyptian linen"
"850","Yahya related to me from Malik that he asked Abdullah ibn Dinar what Abdullah ibn Umar used to do with the drapings of his animals when the Kaba began to be draped with the kiswa"
"851","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say"
"852","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar never used to tear the drapes of his sacrificial animals"
"853","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father used to say to his sons"
"854","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that the man who was in charge of the sacrificial animal of the Messenger of Allah"
"855","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Said ibn al- Musayyab said"
"856","Yahya related to me from Malik from Thawr ibn Zayd ad-Dili from Abdullah ibn Abbas the same as that"
"857","Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab said"
"858","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"859","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard the people of knowledge say"
"860","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that he heard Said ibn al-Musayyab asking a group of people"
"861","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said said that Sulayman ibn Yasar told him that Abu Ayyub al-Ansari once set off to do hajj and then"
"862","Malik related to me from Nafi from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Habbar ibn al-Aswad arrived on the day of sacrifice while Umar ibn al-Khattab was sacrificing his animal and said"
"863","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zubayr al-Makki from Ata ibn Abi Rabah that Abdullah ibn Abbas was asked about a man who had had intercourse with his wife while at Mina before he had done the tawaf al-ifada"
"864","Yahya related to me from Malik from Thawr ibn Zayd ad-Dili that lkrama"
"865","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman saying the same about that as what Ikrama related from Ibn Abbas. Malik said"
"866","Yahya related to me from Malik from Jafar ibn Muhammad from his father that Ali ibn Abi Talib used to say"
"867","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Abbas used to say"
"868","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Urnar used to say"
"869","Yahya related to me from Malik fromAbdullah ibn Abi Bakr that a mawla of Amir bint Abd ar-Rahman called Ruqayya told him that she once set out with Amra bint Abd ar-Rahman to go to Makka. She said"
"870","Yahya related to me from Malik from Sadaqa ibn Yasar al-Makki that a man from the people of Yemen"
"871","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say"
"872","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard one of the people of knowledge say"
"873","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the Messenger of Allah"
